.TH GM\-RUN 1 "2026-09-21" "guildmaster 0.1" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
gm\-run \- run a command under the guildmaster jobserver
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B gm\-run
.I command
.RI [ argument ...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B gm\-run
opens
.IR /dev/guild ,
waits for one token, and runs
.I command
with
.B \-\-jobserver\-auth=fifo:/dev/guild
appended to
.BR MAKEFLAGS ,
so that jobserver-aware tools such as GNU Make and Ninja share the
machine-wide pool. The token is returned when
.I command
finishes.
.PP
The invoking user needs read and write access to
.IR /dev/guild ;
with the packaged udev rules that means membership of the
.B guild
group.
.SH EXIT STATUS
The exit status of
.IR command ;
128 plus the signal number if it was killed by a signal; or 1 if
.I /dev/guild
could not be opened or read, or the command could not be run.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR guildmaster (8)
